/-!
# The exceptional divisor of an affine blowup is an effective Cartier divisor

Let `R` be a commutative ring and `I ⊆ R` an ideal. The blowup of `Spec R` in `I` is
`Stacks.Blowup.blowUpSpec I = Proj (⨁ₙ Iⁿ)`, with structure morphism
`Stacks.Blowup.toSpec I`. This file proves that the inverse image of the closed subscheme
cut out by `I` is an effective Cartier divisor on the blowup.

This is part (2) of Stacks tag 02OS. The Stacks proof of that part begins "the second
statement is local on `X`, hence we may assume `X` affine", so what is proved here is the
whole mathematical content of the part; the remaining step for a general scheme is the
identification of the restriction of a relative `Proj` to an affine open with the `Proj`
built here, which is Stacks tag 0804 and needs relative `Proj` (tags 01NO, 01NQ).

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Blowup.chartAwayMap`: the structure map `R ⟶ (⨁ₙ Iⁿ)_{(a⁽¹⁾)}` of the affine
  blowup chart `D₊(a⁽¹⁾)` attached to an element `a ∈ I`.
* `Stacks.Blowup.chartAwayDiv`: the fraction `b / a` on that chart, for `b ∈ I`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Blowup.map_ideal_chartAwayMap`: on the chart `D₊(a⁽¹⁾)` the ideal generated by the
  image of `I` is generated by the image of the single element `a`.
* `Stacks.Blowup.isRegular_chartAwayMap`: that element is a nonzerodivisor there.
* `Stacks.Blowup.awayι_comp_toSpec`: the chart inclusion followed by the structure morphism
  of the blowup is `Spec` of `Stacks.Blowup.chartAwayMap`.
* `Stacks.Blowup.isEffectiveCartierDivisor_comap_toSpec`: **Stacks tag 02OS part (2) for the
  affine blowup.** The inverse image of the centre under the blowup of `Spec R` in `I` is an
  effective Cartier divisor.
* `Stacks.Blowup.isEffectiveCartierDivisor_comap_toSpec_ofIdealTop`: the same with no
  hypothesis, for the ideal sheaf `Spec R` carries canonically.

## Implementation notes

The two chart facts are the content of Stacks tag 07Z3 for the affine blowup algebra
`R[I/a]`, which is proved for the quotient model `Blowup I a` of
`StacksFrontier/RingTheory/Blowup/Basic.lean` as `blowup_idealMap_eq_span` and
`blowup_image_a_mem_nonZeroDivisors`. They are
reproved here directly inside `HomogeneousLocalization.Away (reesGrading I) a⁽¹⁾`, which is
the ring the chart of `Proj` actually has, rather than by transporting along an
identification of that ring with the quotient model: no such identification is in the
repository (tag 052Q's chart statement, the second half of tag 0804, is not formalized), and
both facts are two-line computations with fractions. The degree-one fraction `b / a` is
`Stacks.Blowup.chartAwayDiv`, and `a` is a nonzerodivisor because `a⁽¹⁾ = a·T` in the Rees
algebra, so multiplying a relation by one further power of `a⁽¹⁾` replaces the factor `a`
by a factor `T`, which is a nonzerodivisor in `R[T]`.

The scheme-level assembly uses the backward half of tag 01WS,
`Stacks.Divisors.isEffectiveCartierDivisor_of_forall_exists_affineOpen`,
together with the covering of the blowup by the standard
opens of the degree-one elements of the Rees algebra
(`Stacks.Blowup.iSup_basicOpen_reesGrading_one_eq_top`). The affine open around a point is
taken to be the *image of the top open* under `AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.awayι` rather than the
standard open itself; the two are equal, but only the former makes
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.ideal_comap_of_isOpenImmersion` apply with no
transport, which is what keeps the proof free of the heterogeneous-equality bookkeeping that
the same computation needs when phrased through `Scheme.Opens.topIso`.

The centre is taken as an arbitrary ideal sheaf `J` on `Spec R` whose ideal of global
sections is `I` read through `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.ΓSpecIso`, rather than as a chosen
ideal sheaf built from `I`. That way a consumer holding its own ideal sheaf — which is the
shape of tag 0806's hypothesis — can use the result without first identifying it with a
construction made here.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 02OS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02OS)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07Z3](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07Z3)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0804](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0804)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01WS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01WS)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory Polynomial HomogeneousLocalization

universe u

namespace Stacks.Blowup

-- `Stacks.Blowup.blowUpSpec` is a plain `def` for `AlgebraicGeometry.Proj (reesGrading I)`, so
-- the two spellings are definitionally but not reducibly equal and `rw`'s `kabstract`, which
-- runs at `implicit` transparency, reports the chart morphisms as not type-correct. This is the
-- repository's sanctioned idiom for that situation; it changes no elaboration option.

attribute [local implicit_reducible] blowUpSpec

variable {R : Type u} [CommRing R] (I : Ideal R) {a : R} (ha : a ∈ I)

/-! ### The affine chart attached to an element of the ideal -/

/-- The structure map of the affine blowup chart `D₊(a⁽¹⁾)` of `Proj (⨁ₙ Iⁿ)`: the composite
of the identification of `R` with the degree-zero part of the Rees algebra with the inclusion
of that degree-zero part into the degree-zero part of the localization at `a⁽¹⁾`. -/
def chartAwayMap : R →+* Away (reesGrading I) (reesDegOne I ha) :=
  (fromZeroRingHom (reesGrading I) (Submonoid.powers (reesDegOne I ha))).comp
    (reesGradingZeroEquiv I).toRingHom

theorem chartAwayMap_val (r : R) : (chartAwayMap I ha r).val =
    Localization.mk ((reesGradingZeroEquiv I r : reesGrading I 0) : reesAlgebra I) 1 := by
  change (HomogeneousLocalization.mk ⟨0, _, 1, _⟩).val = _
  rw [HomogeneousLocalization.val_mk]
  rfl

/-- The degree-zero part of the Rees algebra is a copy of `R`, in which `r` is the constant
polynomial `r`. -/
theorem coe_coe_reesGradingZeroEquiv (r : R) :
    (((reesGradingZeroEquiv I r : reesGrading I 0) : reesAlgebra I) : R[X]) = C r := by
  change ((algebraMap R (reesGrading I 0) r : reesGrading I 0) : reesAlgebra I).1 = C r
  rw [SetLike.GradeZero.coe_algebraMap]
  rfl

/-- The degree-one element `a⁽¹⁾` of the Rees algebra is the polynomial `a·T`, written as a
product rather than as the monomial of `Stacks.Blowup.coe_reesDegOne`. -/
theorem coe_reesDegOne_eq_C_mul_X :
    ((reesDegOne I ha : reesAlgebra I) : R[X]) = C a * Polynomial.X := by
  change (monomial 1 a : R[X]) = C a * Polynomial.X
  rw [← C_mul_X_pow_eq_monomial, pow_one]

/-- The fraction `b / a` on the chart `D₊(a⁽¹⁾)`, for `b ∈ I`: the quotient of the two
degree-one elements `b⁽¹⁾` and `a⁽¹⁾` of the Rees algebra. -/
def chartAwayDiv {b : R} (hb : b ∈ I) : Away (reesGrading I) (reesDegOne I ha) :=
  HomogeneousLocalization.mk
    ⟨1, ⟨reesDegOne I hb, reesDegOne_mem_reesGrading I hb⟩,
      ⟨reesDegOne I ha, reesDegOne_mem_reesGrading I ha⟩, ⟨1, pow_one _⟩⟩

/-- **Every element of the ideal is divisible by `a` on the chart `D₊(a⁽¹⁾)`.** -/
theorem chartAwayMap_eq_mul {b : R} (hb : b ∈ I) :
    chartAwayMap I ha b = chartAwayMap I ha a * chartAwayDiv I ha hb := by
  apply HomogeneousLocalization.val_injective
  rw [HomogeneousLocalization.val_mul, chartAwayMap_val, chartAwayMap_val, chartAwayDiv,
    HomogeneousLocalization.val_mk, Localization.mk_mul,
    Localization.mk_eq_mk_iff, Localization.r_iff_exists]
  refine ⟨1, ?_⟩
  apply Subtype.ext
  simp only [OneMemClass.coe_one, one_mul, Subalgebra.coe_mul, coe_coe_reesGradingZeroEquiv,
    reesDegOne]
  change ((1 : reesAlgebra I) * (reesDegOne I ha) : R[X]) * C b = C a * (monomial 1 b : R[X])
  change (1 : R[X]) * monomial 1 a * C b = C a * monomial 1 b
  rw [one_mul, C_mul_monomial, monomial_mul_C, mul_comm]

/-- **On the chart `D₊(a⁽¹⁾)` the ideal `I` becomes the principal ideal generated by `a`.**
This is clause (2) of Stacks tag 07Z3 for the chart ring of `Proj (⨁ₙ Iⁿ)`. -/
theorem map_ideal_chartAwayMap :
    Ideal.map (chartAwayMap I ha) I = Ideal.span {chartAwayMap I ha a} := by
  refine le_antisymm (Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap.mpr fun b hb ↦ ?_) ?_
  · rw [Ideal.mem_comap, Ideal.mem_span_singleton]
    exact ⟨chartAwayDiv I ha hb, chartAwayMap_eq_mul I ha hb⟩
  · rw [Ideal.span_le, Set.singleton_subset_iff, SetLike.mem_coe]
    exact Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ ha

/-! ### Regularity of the chart generator -/

private theorem mul_eq_zero_imp_eq_zero_loc
    (w : Localization (Submonoid.powers (reesDegOne I ha)))
    (hw : Localization.mk ((reesGradingZeroEquiv I a : reesGrading I 0) : reesAlgebra I) 1 * w
      = 0) : w = 0 := by
  induction w using Localization.induction_on with
  | _ y =>
    obtain ⟨n, d⟩ := y
    rw [Localization.mk_mul, show (0 : Localization
        (Submonoid.powers (reesDegOne I ha))) = Localization.mk 0 1 from
        (Localization.mk_zero _).symm,
      Localization.mk_eq_mk_iff, Localization.r_iff_exists] at hw
    obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := hw
    obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := c.2
    rw [show (0 : Localization (Submonoid.powers (reesDegOne I ha))) = Localization.mk 0 1 from
      (Localization.mk_zero _).symm, Localization.mk_eq_mk_iff, Localization.r_iff_exists]
    refine ⟨⟨reesDegOne I ha ^ (k + 1), ⟨k + 1, rfl⟩⟩, ?_⟩
    simp only [OneMemClass.coe_one, one_mul, mul_zero] at hc ⊢
    apply Subtype.ext
    have hc' : ((reesDegOne I ha : reesAlgebra I) : R[X]) ^ k *
        (((reesGradingZeroEquiv I a : reesGrading I 0) : reesAlgebra I) : R[X]) *
          (n : R[X]) = 0 := by
      have h2 := congrArg (fun w : reesAlgebra I ↦ (w : R[X])) hc
      simpa [← hk, mul_assoc] using h2
    have hgoal : ((reesDegOne I ha : reesAlgebra I) : R[X]) ^ (k + 1) * (n : R[X]) = 0 := by
      rw [coe_reesDegOne_eq_C_mul_X] at hc' ⊢
      rw [coe_coe_reesGradingZeroEquiv] at hc'
      ring_nf at hc' ⊢
      linear_combination Polynomial.X * hc'
    simpa [mul_assoc] using hgoal

/-- **The chart generator is a nonzerodivisor.** This is clause (1) of Stacks tag 07Z3 for the
chart ring of `Proj (⨁ₙ Iⁿ)`. -/
theorem isRegular_chartAwayMap : IsRegular (chartAwayMap I ha a) := by
  have key : ∀ z : Away (reesGrading I) (reesDegOne I ha),
      chartAwayMap I ha a * z = 0 → z = 0 := by
    intro z hz
    apply HomogeneousLocalization.val_injective
    rw [HomogeneousLocalization.val_zero]
    refine mul_eq_zero_imp_eq_zero_loc I ha z.val ?_
    rw [← chartAwayMap_val, ← HomogeneousLocalization.val_mul, hz,
      HomogeneousLocalization.val_zero]
  have hleft : IsLeftRegular (chartAwayMap I ha a) := by
    intro y z hyz
    have h0 : chartAwayMap I ha a * (y - z) = 0 := by
      rw [mul_sub]
      exact sub_eq_zero_of_eq hyz
    exact sub_eq_zero.mp (key _ h0)
  exact (Commute.isRegular_iff (Commute.all _)).2 hleft

/-! ### The chart inclusion over the base -/

/-- **The affine chart of the blowup, over the base.** Composing the open immersion
`Spec (⨁ₙ Iⁿ)_{(a⁽¹⁾)} ⟶ Proj (⨁ₙ Iⁿ)` with the structure morphism of the blowup gives
`Spec` of `Stacks.Blowup.chartAwayMap`. -/
theorem awayι_comp_toSpec :
    Proj.awayι (reesGrading I) (reesDegOne I ha) (reesDegOne_mem_reesGrading I ha) one_pos ≫
        toSpec I =
      Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (chartAwayMap I ha)) := by
  rw [toSpec, ← Category.assoc, Proj.awayι_toSpecZero, ← Spec.map_comp]
  rfl

/-- Pushing an ideal forward along an isomorphism and back along its inverse is the identity. -/
private theorem map_map_hom_inv {A B : CommRingCat.{u}} (e : A ≅ B) (K : Ideal B) :
    Ideal.map e.hom.hom (Ideal.map e.inv.hom K) = K := by
  rw [Ideal.map_map, ← CommRingCat.hom_comp, Iso.inv_hom_id, CommRingCat.hom_id, Ideal.map_id]

/-- The ideal of global sections of the inverse image of an ideal sheaf on an affine scheme along
`Spec` of a ring map, with both identifications `Γ(Spec R, ⊤) ≅ R` carried out. Stated at
abstract rings and applied, rather than rewritten in place. -/
private theorem ideal_comap_SpecMap_top {R₁ R₂ : CommRingCat.{u}} (φ : R₁ ⟶ R₂)
    (J : (Spec R₁).IdealSheafData) (K : Ideal R₁)
    (hJ : J.ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩ = Ideal.map (Scheme.ΓSpecIso R₁).inv.hom K) :
    (J.comap (Spec.map φ)).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩ =
      Ideal.map (Scheme.ΓSpecIso R₂).inv.hom (Ideal.map φ.hom K) := by
  have happ : (Spec.map φ).appTop =
      ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso R₁).hom ≫ φ) ≫ (Scheme.ΓSpecIso R₂).inv := by
    rw [Iso.eq_comp_inv]
    exact Scheme.ΓSpecIso_naturality _
  rw [Stacks.IdealSheaf.ideal_comap_top_of_isAffine, hJ, happ, CommRingCat.hom_comp,
    CommRingCat.hom_comp, ← Ideal.map_map, ← Ideal.map_map,
    map_map_hom_inv]

/-! ### Tag 02OS part (2) for the affine blowup -/

private theorem isRegular_iso_apply {A B : CommRingCat.{u}} (e : A ≅ B) {x : A}
    (hx : IsRegular x) : IsRegular (e.hom.hom x) :=
  Stacks.Divisors.isRegular_ringEquiv e.commRingCatIsoToRingEquiv hx

/-- Stated at abstract rings and applied, rather than rewritten in place: the carriers below are
sections of the blowup, whose `whnf` is large, and `rw` has to unfold them to find the pattern. -/
public theorem map_span_singleton {A B : CommRingCat.{u}} (f : A ⟶ B) (x : A) :
    Ideal.map f.hom (Ideal.span {x}) = Ideal.span {f.hom x} := by
  rw [Ideal.map_span, Set.image_singleton]

private theorem map_span_singleton_iso {A B : CommRingCat.{u}} (e : A ≅ B) (x : B) :
    Ideal.map e.hom.hom (Ideal.span {e.inv.hom x}) = Ideal.span {x} := by
  rw [map_span_singleton, ← CommRingCat.comp_apply, e.inv_hom_id, CommRingCat.id_apply]

/-- If the inverse image of an ideal sheaf along an open immersion `j` of an affine scheme is
generated by `x` on the top open, then the ideal on the image of `j` is generated by `x`, read
through the identifications of the sections. -/
private theorem ideal_image_top_eq_span {Y : Scheme.{u}} (K : Y.IdealSheafData)
    {B : CommRingCat.{u}} (j : Spec B ⟶ Y) [IsOpenImmersion j] (x : B)
    (h : (K.comap j).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩ =
      Ideal.span {(Scheme.ΓSpecIso B).inv.hom x}) :
    K.ideal ⟨j ''ᵁ ⊤, (isAffineOpen_top _).image_of_isOpenImmersion j⟩ =
      Ideal.span {(j.appIso ⊤).inv.hom ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso B).inv.hom x)} := by
  refine Stacks.IdealSheaf.ideal_map_hom_injective (j.appIso ⊤) (Eq.trans ?_
    (map_span_singleton_iso (j.appIso ⊤) _).symm)
  exact (Stacks.IdealSheaf.ideal_map_hom_eq_comap_inv (j.appIso ⊤) _).trans
    ((Scheme.IdealSheafData.ideal_comap_of_isOpenImmersion K j ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩).symm.trans
      h)

/-- The chart inclusion `Spec (⨁ₙ Iⁿ)_{(b⁽¹⁾)} ⟶ Proj (⨁ₙ Iⁿ)` of the affine blowup.

The name is not `chartι`: `Stacks.RelativeProj.Data.chartι` is the chart inclusion of a
relative `Proj`, a different notion, and the two should not share a short name. -/
abbrev awayChartι {b : R} (hb : b ∈ I) :
    Spec (CommRingCat.of (Away (reesGrading I) (reesDegOne I hb))) ⟶ blowUpSpec I :=
  Proj.awayι (reesGrading I) (reesDegOne I hb) (reesDegOne_mem_reesGrading I hb) one_pos

/-- The affine open of the blowup underlying the chart attached to `b ∈ I`: the image of the
top open under the chart inclusion. It is the standard open `D₊(b⁽¹⁾)` — see
`Stacks.Blowup.chartImage_eq_basicOpen` — but this spelling is the one for which
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.ideal_comap_of_isOpenImmersion` applies with no
transport. -/
def chartImage {b : R} (hb : b ∈ I) : (blowUpSpec I).Opens := awayChartι I hb ''ᵁ ⊤

theorem chartImage_eq_basicOpen {b : R} (hb : b ∈ I) :
    chartImage I hb = Proj.basicOpen (reesGrading I) (reesDegOne I hb) := by
  rw [chartImage, Scheme.Hom.image_top_eq_opensRange]
  exact Proj.opensRange_awayι _ _ _ _

theorem isAffineOpen_chartImage {b : R} (hb : b ∈ I) : IsAffineOpen (chartImage I hb) :=
  (isAffineOpen_top _).image_of_isOpenImmersion _

attribute [local implicit_reducible] chartImage

/-- The sections of the blowup over the chart `D₊(b⁽¹⁾)`, identified with the degree-zero part
of the localization of the Rees algebra at `b⁽¹⁾`. -/
abbrev chartSections {b : R} (hb : b ∈ I) :
    Γ(blowUpSpec I, chartImage I hb) ≅
      Γ(Spec (CommRingCat.of (Away (reesGrading I) (reesDegOne I hb))), ⊤) :=
  (awayChartι I hb).appIso ⊤

/-- The global sections of the spectrum of the chart ring, identified with that ring. -/
abbrev chartGamma {b : R} (hb : b ∈ I) :
    Γ(Spec (CommRingCat.of (Away (reesGrading I) (reesDegOne I hb))), ⊤) ≅
      CommRingCat.of (Away (reesGrading I) (reesDegOne I hb)) :=
  Scheme.ΓSpecIso _

/-- The generator of the inverse image of the centre on the chart `D₊(b⁽¹⁾)`: the image of `b`
under the identification of the sections over the chart with the chart ring. -/
def chartGenerator {b : R} (hb : b ∈ I) : Γ(blowUpSpec I, chartImage I hb) :=
  (chartSections I hb).inv.hom ((chartGamma I hb).inv.hom (chartAwayMap I hb b))

/-- **The chart generator is a nonzerodivisor.** This is clause (1) of tag 07Z3, transported
along the two identifications. -/
theorem isRegular_chartGenerator {b : R} (hb : b ∈ I) : IsRegular (chartGenerator I hb) :=
  isRegular_iso_apply (chartSections I hb).symm
    (isRegular_iso_apply (chartGamma I hb).symm (isRegular_chartAwayMap I hb))

/-- **The inverse image of the centre on the chart `D₊(b⁽¹⁾)` is generated by the chart
generator.** This is the affine-local input of tag 01WS at the chart, with the generator named
rather than existentially quantified, and it is where the two chart facts of tag 07Z3 are used. -/
theorem ideal_comap_toSpec_eq_span_chartGenerator
    (J : (Spec (CommRingCat.of R)).IdealSheafData)
    (hJ : Ideal.map (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of R)).hom.hom
        (J.ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩) = I) {b : R} (hb : b ∈ I) :
    (J.comap (toSpec I)).ideal ⟨chartImage I hb, isAffineOpen_chartImage I hb⟩ =
      Ideal.span {chartGenerator I hb} := by
  have hJ' : J.ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩ =
      Ideal.map (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of R)).inv.hom I := by
    rw [← hJ]
    exact (map_map_hom_inv (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of R)).symm _).symm
  refine ideal_image_top_eq_span (J.comap (toSpec I)) (awayChartι I hb) (chartAwayMap I hb b) ?_
  rw [← Scheme.IdealSheafData.comap_comp, awayι_comp_toSpec,
    ideal_comap_SpecMap_top _ J I hJ', CommRingCat.hom_ofHom, map_ideal_chartAwayMap]
  exact map_span_singleton (Scheme.ΓSpecIso _).inv _

/-- **The inverse image of the centre is principal on the chart `D₊(b⁽¹⁾)`, generated by a
nonzerodivisor.** This is the affine-local input of tag 01WS at the chart, and it is where the
two chart facts of tag 07Z3 are used. -/
theorem exists_isRegular_ideal_comap_toSpec_eq_span
    (J : (Spec (CommRingCat.of R)).IdealSheafData)
    (hJ : Ideal.map (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of R)).hom.hom
        (J.ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩) = I) {b : R} (hb : b ∈ I) :
    ∃ g : Γ(blowUpSpec I, chartImage I hb), IsRegular g ∧
      (J.comap (toSpec I)).ideal ⟨chartImage I hb, isAffineOpen_chartImage I hb⟩ =
        Ideal.span {g} :=
  ⟨chartGenerator I hb, isRegular_chartGenerator I hb,
    ideal_comap_toSpec_eq_span_chartGenerator I J hJ hb⟩

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 02OS part (2), for the affine blowup.** Let `I ⊆ R` be an ideal and
let `J` be the ideal sheaf on `Spec R` cut out by `I`. The inverse image of `J` under the
blowup morphism `Proj (⨁ₙ Iⁿ) ⟶ Spec R` is an effective Cartier divisor.

The blowup is covered by the standard opens `D₊(a⁽¹⁾)` for `a ∈ I`, whose chart rings are the
affine blowup algebras `R[I/a]`; on each of them the inverse image of `I` is generated by the
single nonzerodivisor `a`, which is the affine-local criterion of tag 01WS. -/
theorem isEffectiveCartierDivisor_comap_toSpec
    (J : (Spec (CommRingCat.of R)).IdealSheafData)
    (hJ : Ideal.map (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of R)).hom.hom
        (J.ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩) = I) :
    Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor (J.comap (toSpec I)) := by
  refine Stacks.Divisors.isEffectiveCartierDivisor_of_forall_exists_affineOpen _ fun y ↦ ?_
  -- a degree-one standard open containing `y`
  obtain ⟨f, hyf⟩ : ∃ f : reesGrading I 1,
      y ∈ Proj.basicOpen (reesGrading I) ((f : reesAlgebra I)) := by
    have hcov := iSup_basicOpen_reesGrading_one_eq_top I
    have hy : y ∈ (⊤ : (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj (reesGrading I)).Opens) := trivial
    rw [← hcov] at hy
    exact TopologicalSpace.Opens.mem_iSup.mp hy
  -- it is the chart of an element of `I`; `b` is kept opaque so that the chart computation,
  -- which is a separate lemma in `b`, applies without unfolding a local definition
  obtain ⟨b, hb, hfeq⟩ : ∃ (b : R) (hb : b ∈ I), (f : reesAlgebra I) = reesDegOne I hb := by
    refine ⟨((f : reesAlgebra I) : R[X]).coeff 1, by simpa [pow_one] using (f : reesAlgebra I).2 1,
      ?_⟩
    exact Subtype.ext (coe_eq_monomial I f.2)
  rw [hfeq] at hyf
  obtain ⟨g, hgreg, hgspan⟩ := exists_isRegular_ideal_comap_toSpec_eq_span I J hJ hb
  refine ⟨chartImage I hb, isAffineOpen_chartImage I hb, ?_, g, hgreg, hgspan⟩
  rw [chartImage_eq_basicOpen]
  exact hyf

/-- The ideal sheaf on `Spec R` attached to `I` through `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.ΓSpecIso`
satisfies the hypothesis the results above make on the centre. -/
theorem map_ideal_ofIdealTop_comap_eq :
    Ideal.map (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of R)).hom.hom
        ((Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop
          (Ideal.comap (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of R)).hom.hom I)).ideal
            ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩) = I := by
  have hKtop : (Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop
      (Ideal.comap (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of R)).hom.hom I)).ideal
        ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top (Spec (CommRingCat.of R))⟩ =
      Ideal.comap (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of R)).hom.hom I := by
    rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop_ideal,
      show (homOfLE (le_top (a := (⊤ : (Spec (CommRingCat.of R)).Opens)))) = 𝟙 _ from rfl]
    simp
  rw [hKtop]
  exact Ideal.map_comap_of_surjective _
    (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of R)).commRingCatIsoToRingEquiv.surjective I

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 02OS part (2), for the affine blowup**, with no hypothesis: the
centre is the ideal sheaf on `Spec R` attached to `I` through
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.ΓSpecIso`. -/
theorem isEffectiveCartierDivisor_comap_toSpec_ofIdealTop :
    Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor
      ((Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop
        (Ideal.comap (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of R)).hom.hom I)).comap (toSpec I)) :=
  isEffectiveCartierDivisor_comap_toSpec I _ (map_ideal_ofIdealTop_comap_eq I)

/-! ### Tag 07Z3 for the localization model of the affine blowup algebra

`AlgebraicGeometry.affineBlowupStandardOpenIso` presents the chart of a blowup as the spectrum
of `affineBlowupAlgebra J c S`, the subalgebra of a localization `S` of `A` away from `c`
generated by the fractions `b / c` with `b ∈ J`. The two facts of tag 07Z3 are cheaper for this
model than for the quotient model `Blowup J c` they are proved for: the fraction `b / c` is one
of the *generators*, and `c` is a *unit* in `S`, so it is a nonzerodivisor on any subring.
-/

section AffineBlowupAlgebra

variable {A : Type u} [CommRing A] (J : Ideal A) (c : A)
  (S : Type u) [CommRing S] [Algebra A S] [IsLocalization.Away c S]

/-- **Clause (2) of Stacks tag 07Z3 for the localization model.** In `A[J/c]` the ideal
generated by the image of `J` is generated by the image of `c`. -/
theorem map_ideal_algebraMap_affineBlowupAlgebra (hc : c ∈ J) :
    Ideal.map (algebraMap A (affineBlowupAlgebra J c S)) J =
      Ideal.span {algebraMap A (affineBlowupAlgebra J c S) c} := by
  refine le_antisymm (Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap.mpr fun b hb ↦ ?_) ?_
  · rw [Ideal.mem_comap, Ideal.mem_span_singleton]
    exact ⟨affineBlowupFraction J c S hb, (algebraMap_mul_affineBlowupFraction J c S hb).symm⟩
  · rw [Ideal.span_le, Set.singleton_subset_iff, SetLike.mem_coe]
    exact Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ hc

/-- **Clause (1) of Stacks tag 07Z3 for the localization model.** The image of `c` in `A[J/c]`
is a nonzerodivisor, because `c` is a unit in the ambient localization. -/
theorem isRegular_algebraMap_affineBlowupAlgebra :
    IsRegular (algebraMap A (affineBlowupAlgebra J c S) c) := by
  have hunit : IsUnit ((algebraMap A S) c) := IsLocalization.Away.algebraMap_isUnit c
  have hcoe : ∀ x : affineBlowupAlgebra J c S,
      ((algebraMap A (affineBlowupAlgebra J c S) c * x : affineBlowupAlgebra J c S) : S) =
        (algebraMap A S) c * (x : S) := fun x ↦ by
    rw [Subalgebra.coe_mul]
    congr 1
  have hleft : IsLeftRegular (algebraMap A (affineBlowupAlgebra J c S) c) := by
    intro x z hxz
    apply Subtype.ext
    refine hunit.mul_left_cancel ?_
    rw [← hcoe x, ← hcoe z]
    exact congrArg (fun w : affineBlowupAlgebra J c S ↦ (w : S)) hxz
  exact (Commute.isRegular_iff (Commute.all _)).2 hleft

end AffineBlowupAlgebra

/-! ### Tag 02OS part (2) for an arbitrary scheme

The blowup `AlgebraicGeometry.blowUp I` of `X` in `I` is the relative `Proj` of the Rees
algebra (Tag 01OG), which Tag 01NQ constructs unconditionally, and
`AlgebraicGeometry.blownUpAffine_chart_cover` (Tag 0804) covers the part of it lying over an
affine open `U` of the base by the spectra of the affine blowup algebras
`Γ(X, U)[I(U)/a]` for `a ∈ I(U)`. On each of those the inverse image of the centre is the
principal ideal generated by the nonzerodivisor `a`, which is the affine-local criterion of
Tag 01WS.

The chart itself is not built here: it is `Stacks.BlowUpChartCover.chart`, with
`Stacks.BlowUpChartCover.isOpenImmersion_chart`,
`Stacks.BlowUpChartCover.chart_blowUpToBase` and `Stacks.BlowUpChartCover.range_chart`.
-/

/-- The ideal of global sections of the inverse image of an ideal sheaf along
`Spec Γ(X, U) ⟶ X` for an affine open `U` is the ideal of `U`, read through
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.ΓSpecIso`.

The affineness of `U` is taken as an explicit argument rather than read off `U.2`: the two are
the same statement, but only this spelling has `IsAffineOpen` as its *type*, which is what the
`rw` with `AlgebraicGeometry.IsAffineOpen.isoSpec_inv_appTop` needs in order to match. -/
private theorem ideal_comap_isoSpec_inv_top {X : Scheme.{u}} (I : X.IdealSheafData)
    (U : X.affineOpens) (hU : IsAffineOpen (U : X.Opens)) :
    ((I.comap (U : X.Opens).ι).comap hU.isoSpec.inv).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩ =
      Ideal.map (Scheme.ΓSpecIso Γ(X, (U : X.Opens))).inv.hom (I.ideal U) := by
  have hUaff : IsAffine (U : X.Opens).toScheme := hU
  have h2 : Ideal.map (Scheme.Hom.appTop hU.isoSpec.inv).hom
      (Ideal.map (U : X.Opens).topIso.inv.hom (I.ideal U)) =
      Ideal.map (Scheme.ΓSpecIso Γ(X, (U : X.Opens))).inv.hom (I.ideal U) := by
    rw [IsAffineOpen.isoSpec_inv_appTop, CommRingCat.hom_comp, ← Ideal.map_map,
      map_map_hom_inv]
  have h1 := Stacks.IdealSheaf.ideal_comap_top_of_isAffine (I.comap (U : X.Opens).ι)
    hU.isoSpec.inv
  rw [Stacks.IdealSheaf.ideal_comap_ι_top I hU (isAffineOpen_top _)] at h1
  exact h1.trans h2

/-- **The generic chart computation.** Let `I` be an ideal sheaf on `Z`, let `b : Y ⟶ Z`, and let
`j` be an open immersion of an affine scheme `Spec B` into `Y` whose composite with `b` is
`Spec` of a ring map `φ : Γ(Z, U) ⟶ B` followed by `Spec Γ(Z, U) ⟶ Z`, for an affine open `U`
of `Z`. If the image of `I(U)` under `φ` is principal on a regular element, then the inverse
image of `I` under `b` is principal on a regular element over the image of `j`.

Everything is a parameter: `Y`, `b`, `B` and `j` are opaque, so `isDefEq` cannot unfold them.
Stating this at the blowup instead makes the same proof time out, because
`AlgebraicGeometry.exceptionalIdeal`, `AlgebraicGeometry.blowUpToBase` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.reesSituation` are all `abbrev`s and therefore reducible. -/
private theorem exists_isRegular_of_chart {Z Y : Scheme.{u}} (I : Z.IdealSheafData) (b : Y ⟶ Z)
    {B : Type u} [CommRing B] (j : Spec (CommRingCat.of B) ⟶ Y) [IsOpenImmersion j]
    (U : Z.affineOpens) (hU : IsAffineOpen (U : Z.Opens))
    (φ : Γ(Z, (U : Z.Opens)) ⟶ CommRingCat.of B)
    (hover : j ≫ b = Spec.map φ ≫ hU.fromSpec)
    (t : Γ(Z, (U : Z.Opens)))
    (hspan : Ideal.map φ.hom (I.ideal U) = Ideal.span {φ.hom t})
    (hreg : IsRegular (φ.hom t)) :
    ∃ g : Γ(Y, j ''ᵁ ⊤), IsRegular g ∧
      (I.comap b).ideal ⟨j ''ᵁ ⊤, (isAffineOpen_top _).image_of_isOpenImmersion j⟩ =
        Ideal.span {g} := by
  refine ⟨(j.appIso ⊤).inv.hom ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of B)).inv.hom (φ.hom t)), ?_, ?_⟩
  · exact isRegular_iso_apply (j.appIso ⊤).symm
      (isRegular_iso_apply (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of B)).symm hreg)
  have hcomap : (I.comap b).comap j = (I.comap hU.fromSpec).comap (Spec.map φ) := by
    rw [show (I.comap b).comap j = I.comap (j ≫ b) from
        (Scheme.IdealSheafData.comap_comp I j b).symm, hover,
      Scheme.IdealSheafData.comap_comp]
  have hbase : (I.comap hU.fromSpec).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩ =
      Ideal.map (Scheme.ΓSpecIso Γ(Z, (U : Z.Opens))).inv.hom (I.ideal U) := by
    rw [show hU.fromSpec = hU.isoSpec.inv ≫ (U : Z.Opens).ι from rfl,
      Scheme.IdealSheafData.comap_comp]
    exact ideal_comap_isoSpec_inv_top I U hU
  have hstep : ((I.comap b).comap j).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩ =
      Ideal.span {(Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of B)).inv.hom (φ.hom t)} := by
    rw [hcomap, ideal_comap_SpecMap_top φ _ (I.ideal U) hbase, hspan]
    exact map_span_singleton _ _
  exact ideal_image_top_eq_span (I.comap b) j _ hstep

/-- **The exceptional divisor is principal on a standard affine chart, generated by a
nonzerodivisor.** This is the affine-local input of Tag 01WS at the chart of Tag 0804. -/
theorem exists_isRegular_ideal_exceptionalIdeal_eq_span {X : Scheme.{u}}
    (I : X.IdealSheafData) (U : X.affineOpens) (a : I.ideal U) :
    ∃ (V : (AlgebraicGeometry.blowUp I).Opens) (hV : IsAffineOpen V),
      (V : Set (AlgebraicGeometry.blowUp I)) = Set.range ((Proj.basicOpen
          ((AlgebraicGeometry.reesSituation I).sectionRingGrading (U : X.Opens))
            (reesDegreeOne I U a).1).ι ≫ (AlgebraicGeometry.reesSituation I).relativeProjChart U) ∧
        ∃ g : Γ(AlgebraicGeometry.blowUp I, V), IsRegular g ∧
          (exceptionalIdeal I).ideal ⟨V, hV⟩ = Ideal.span {g} := by
  refine ⟨Stacks.BlowUpChartCover.chart I U a ''ᵁ ⊤,
    (isAffineOpen_top _).image_of_isOpenImmersion _, ?_, ?_⟩
  · rw [Scheme.Hom.image_top_eq_opensRange]
    exact Stacks.BlowUpChartCover.range_chart I U a
  exact exists_isRegular_of_chart I (blowUpToBase I) (Stacks.BlowUpChartCover.chart I U a) U U.2
    (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap Γ(X, (U : X.Opens)) _))
    (Stacks.BlowUpChartCover.chart_blowUpToBase I U a) (a : Γ(X, (U : X.Opens)))
    (by rw [CommRingCat.hom_ofHom]
        exact map_ideal_algebraMap_affineBlowupAlgebra (I.ideal U)
          (a : Γ(X, (U : X.Opens))) _ a.2)
    (by rw [CommRingCat.hom_ofHom]
        exact isRegular_algebraMap_affineBlowupAlgebra (I.ideal U)
          (a : Γ(X, (U : X.Opens))) _)

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 02OS part (2).** For a scheme `X` and a quasi-coherent ideal sheaf
`I`, the exceptional divisor of the blowup of `X` in `I` — the inverse image of the closed
subscheme cut out by `I` — is an effective Cartier divisor on the blowup.

Declared as an `instance`, as the tagged statement has it: the head is the ideal sheaf of the
exceptional divisor, so instance search is not widened. -/
@[stacks 02OS "exceptional_effective_cartier", ega "IV 19.4.1"]
instance isEffectiveCartierDivisor_exceptionalIdeal {X : Scheme.{u}} (I : X.IdealSheafData) :
    Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor (exceptionalIdeal I) := by
  refine Stacks.Divisors.isEffectiveCartierDivisor_of_forall_exists_affineOpen _ fun y ↦ ?_
  -- an affine open of the base containing the image of `y`
  have hmem : blowUpToBase I y ∈ (⨆ U : X.affineOpens, (U : X.Opens)) := by
    rw [iSup_affineOpens_eq_top]
    trivial
  obtain ⟨U, hyU⟩ := TopologicalSpace.Opens.mem_iSup.mp hmem
  -- `y` lies on the standard chart of some section of the ideal
  have hy : y ∈ (blowUpToBase I ⁻¹ᵁ (U : X.Opens)).carrier := hyU
  rw [← blownUpAffine_chart_cover I U] at hy
  obtain ⟨a, hya⟩ := Set.mem_iUnion.mp hy
  obtain ⟨V, hV, hVrange, g, hgreg, hgspan⟩ :=
    exists_isRegular_ideal_exceptionalIdeal_eq_span I U a
  refine ⟨V, hV, ?_, g, hgreg, hgspan⟩
  change y ∈ (V : Set (AlgebraicGeometry.blowUp I))
  rw [hVrange]
  exact hya

end Stacks.Blowup

end
